---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Replace a template's body.
The old body is lost, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst template edit <template> <body> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  template   The template: id or name
  body       The new body: a JSON string, @file to read a file, - for stdin

FLAGS
  -y, --yes       Confirm a risky change; a terminal asks instead; without one only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run   Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst tpl edit "Retro" @body.json -y
  $ holst tpl edit "Retro" @body.json -n

LEARN MORE
  A template is given as its id or its name.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
